\section{The Compatible Intersection at the Terminal Time}\label{sec:TheCompatibleIntersectionAtTheTerminalTime}

The tower places every temporal rung beside every spatial row opened by the same pressure-complete history.
The datum-generated producer places every finite rectangle across the whole alleged terminal interval.
Compatibility keeps their shared coordinates identical, so the rectangles form one projective family.
Their intersection reaches one smooth endpoint.
The pressure-explicit recurrence identifies the terminal jet there, and local uniqueness restarts the original history.

